            <ArticleTitle>Cutting Balloon angioplasty for underexpanded stent deployed through struts of previously implanted stent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>697-701</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case in which stenting through the struts of a previously deployed stent resulted in stent underexpansion despite 25 atm inflation pressure. Four months later, follow-up angiography demonstrated in-stent restenosis. It was successfully expanded with a Cutting Balloon.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
